@baseUrl = http://localhost:5050/api
@eventId = 68bc3acd967afbc1b243b2e6
# If using Bearer tokens, paste the JWT here:
@authToken = REPLACE_WITH_JWT
# For a second test user:
@authToken2 = REPLACE_WITH_JWT_2

### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Health (if you have one)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Auth: Register user #1
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Test One",
  "username": "test_one",
  "email": "test1@example.com",
  "password": "12345678"
}

### Auth: Login user #1 (capture cookie/JWT as your app returns)
# If your login returns a token, copy it into {{authToken}} above
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test1@mail.com",
  "password": "1234"
}

### Optional: set initial global interests for user #1
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/me/interests
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "interests": ["AI", "DevOps", "Design Systems", "Product"]
}

### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Get Event by slug (sanity)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/eventhive-2026


### Apply to event (creates EventMember) — user #1
POST {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/apply
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Get my membership for this event — user #1
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Update my per-event attendee profile — user #1
PUT {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/attendee/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bio": "Product-minded engineer. Building AI tooling.",
  "avatarOverride": "https://picsum.photos/seed/u1/200",
  "interests": ["ai", "product", "design systems", "devops"]
}

### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Auth: Register user #2
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Test Two",
  "username": "test_two",
  "email": "test2@mail.com",
  "password": "1234"
}

### Auth: Login user #2 (paste token into {{authToken2}})
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test2@mail.com",
  "password": "1234"
}

### Optional: set initial global interests for user #2
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/me/interests
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken2}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "interests": ["ai", "cloud", "security", "frontend"]
}

### Apply to event — user #2
POST {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/apply
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken2}}

### Update per-event attendee profile — user #2
PUT {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/attendee/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken2}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bio": "Security-focused frontend dev.",
  "avatarOverride": "https://picsum.photos/seed/u2/200",
  "interests": ["ai", "security", "frontend", "cloud"]
}

### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Tags suggestion (autocomplete) — popularity first
GET {{baseUrl}}/tags/suggest?eventId={{eventId}}&q=ai

### Organizer/attendee list (browse) with filters (from Step-2 list endpoint)
# If you restricted this to organizers, use an organizer token
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/attendees?status=approved&role=attendee&q=test&page=1&limit=10&sort=-createdAt
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Matchmaking suggestions (Step-3 Jaccard) — user #1
# NOTE: Requires both users to be "approved" attendees.
# If your apply endpoint defaults to "pending", temporarily set them to "approved" in DB
# or add an admin approve route before running this.
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/match/suggestions?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Matchmaking suggestions — user #2
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/match/suggestions?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken2}}

### Search attendees (Step-3 browse)
# query + tags (ANY by default). Use &match=all for ALL tags.
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/attendees?query=security&tags=ai,frontend&page=1&limit=20&sort=-updatedAt
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken2}}

### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Alternative auth style using cookies (if your backend sets HttpOnly cookies)
# Just omit the Authorization header and let Cookie header carry the session.
# Example (uncomment & replace your cookie):
# GET {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/me
# Cookie: connect.sid=REPLACE_ME; Path=/; HttpOnly; Secure
